\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the Paper2Repro workflow as a stage-wise codebase transformation. From the input paper $R$, two paths proceed and later converge. The \textbf  {build path} (top) materializes and repairs the repository: Paper $\rightarrow $ \textbf  {Plan} $\rightarrow $ \textbf  {Codebase} $\rightarrow $ \textbf  {Iteratively-Fixed Codebase}. The \textbf  {evaluation path} (left) derives the paper-grounded standard: from $R$ we first \emph  {select a small, feasible baseline} to build an \textbf  {Evaluation Plan}, which conditions the \textbf  {Rubric}. The rubric is the hub of the workflow: it drives the in-place repair of the build path via \emph  {hard-coded rubric items}, it is operationalized into the \textbf  {Unit Test} suite, and it supplies \emph  {dataset-loading information} that grows the \textbf  {Codebase with dataset runner}. The dataset-runner codebase and the unit tests converge in \textbf  {Codebase in Docker}, where a \emph  {runtime evaluation-and-fix} loop produces the portable, gradeable \textbf  {Final Codebase}. Each stage either \emph  {creates} structure, \emph  {rewrites} existing files in place, or \emph  {packages} the repository without touching its source (Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:method-stages}).\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:workflow}{{1}{4}{Overview of the Paper2Repro workflow as a stage-wise codebase transformation. From the input paper $R$, two paths proceed and later converge. The \textbf {build path} (top) materializes and repairs the repository: Paper $\rightarrow $ \textbf {Plan} $\rightarrow $ \textbf {Codebase} $\rightarrow $ \textbf {Iteratively-Fixed Codebase}. The \textbf {evaluation path} (left) derives the paper-grounded standard: from $R$ we first \emph {select a small, feasible baseline} to build an \textbf {Evaluation Plan}, which conditions the \textbf {Rubric}. The rubric is the hub of the workflow: it drives the in-place repair of the build path via \emph {hard-coded rubric items}, it is operationalized into the \textbf {Unit Test} suite, and it supplies \emph {dataset-loading information} that grows the \textbf {Codebase with dataset runner}. The dataset-runner codebase and the unit tests converge in \textbf {Codebase in Docker}, where a \emph {runtime evaluation-and-fix} loop produces the portable, gradeable \textbf {Final Codebase}. Each stage either \emph {creates} structure, \emph {rewrites} existing files in place, or \emph {packages} the repository without touching its source (Section~\ref {sec:method-stages}).\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
